},"bed":{"verdict":"within","state":"range","min":50,"max":80,"profileId":"P1188"},"chamber":{"verdict":"within","state":"unknown","min":null,"max":null,"profileId":null},"enclosure":null,"drying":{"need":"required","c":[null,60],"h":[6,8],"hoursOpen":false,"profileId":"P1188"},"hardened":null,"anneal":[],"advice":null,"from":{"chamber":{"kind":"kind","said":"its kind of plastic"}},"profileIds":["P1188","P1423"],"fromId":{"chamber":"CN13"},"replaced":{"nozzle":["P1423"],"bed":["P1423"],"drying":["P1423"]}},"ledger":{"hdt045":[{"rule":"CV05","kind":"demote-to-ceiling","deciding":true,"level":"comparable","lo":null,"hi":78,"measurementId":"V011308","value":74}],"tensileModulusXY":[{"rule":"CV08","kind":"band","deciding":true,"level":"set-apart","lo":3.312,"hi":13.896,"measurementId":"V011305","value":7.2},{"rule":"CV60","kind":"demote-to-ceiling","deciding":false,"level":"comparable","lo":null,"hi":8.12,"measurementId":"V011303","value":7,"factor":1.16}],"tensileStrengthXY":[{"rule":"CV61","kind":"demote-to-ceiling","deciding":false,"level":"comparable","lo":null,"hi":75.4,"measurementId":"V011302","value":65,"factor":1.16}]},"price":null,"notes":[{"topic":"Good for","items":[{"id":"Q06774","text":"Thanks to its heat resistance and stiffness, HI-TEMP CF is ideal for 3D printing lightweight, functional parts like patterns, molds, and tooling.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06778","text":"It can be used as a lightweight alternative to certain metal parts.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06779","text":"BigRep HI-TEMP CF has a heat deflection temperature (HDT B) of up to 74 °C, making it suitable for some applications with limited heat exposure.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06794","text":"They turned to SFM Technology for the solution, resulting in the first 3D-printed main rotor blade restraint cradle, which was printed using BigRep's HI-TEMP CF.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q06775","text":"BigRep’s HI-TEMP CF is a PLA blend reinforced with 10% chopped carbon fiber to increase stiffness and strength.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06776","text":"It has a good strength-to-weight ratio and has been optimized for large-format extrusion.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06777","text":"With a tensile strength of 65 MPa, BigRep HI-TEMP CF can withstand significant stresses and loads without breaking.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06786","text":"HI-TEMP CF is stronger and more durable than PLA and can better withstand impacts without breaking.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06787","text":"It is reinforced with 10% carbon fiber and therefore much stiffer than PLA.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06788","text":"HI-TEMP CF is more heat resistant than PLA with a higher HDT B (74°C vs 54 °C).","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Pitfalls and limitations","items":[{"id":"Q06780","text":"HI-TEMP CF is recommended for indoor use and is susceptible to some chemical degradation.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06781","text":"It is recommended to avoid exposure to strong oxidizing agents and strong acids.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q06784","text":"HI-TEMP CF is a moderately hygroscopic material which means it absorbs moisture from the air which affects the print quality.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06785","text":"We recommend filament storage with a dryer such as the DRYCON which keeps the filament in perfect condition.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06789","text":"Yes, drying HI-TEMP CF filament is important if it has been exposed to moisture.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06790","text":"HI-TEMP CF can absorb water from the air resulting in bubbling or stringing while printing with it.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06791","text":"We recommend using the BigRep DRYCON for 4-6 hours at 50°C, or use any industrial filament dryer or store it in a dry, airtight container with desiccants.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06792","text":"HI-TEMP CF filament has a long shelf life if stored properly in a cool, dry place with minimal exposure to moisture or UV light.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06793","text":"Drying recommendations 60 °C for 6 - 8 hours","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07082","text":"Drying Recommendations 60 °C for 6 - 8 hours","source":"R-BIGREP-EZBYxVrNV7NGt4xXE3UWWuwBPYBbMpjmGobs-fcxZTeadg","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Odour and emissions","items":[{"id":"Q06783","text":"Yes, it is, as long as the room has good ventilation or an air filtration system for the safety and comfort of the people using the 3D printer.","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q06782","text":"Yes, the BigRep HI-TEMP CF is compatible with all open material system 3D printers with a heated print bed and adequate temperature extrusion capabilities (210-240°C).","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q06934","text":"Fan Speed 50 - 100 %","source":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]}],"layers":[],"published":[{"property":"Fibre content","domain":"physical","unit":"%","products":2,"lo":10,"hi":10,"median":10,"values":[10,10]},{"property":"Melting temperature","domain":"thermal","unit":"°C","products":2,"lo":180,"hi":210,"median":187.5,"values":[180,195]},{"property":"Vicat softening temperature","domain":"thermal","unit":"°C","products":2,"lo":165,"hi":165,"median":165,"values":[165,165]},{"property":"Decomposition temperature","domain":"thermal","unit":"°C","products":1,"lo":240,"hi":240,"median":240,"values":[240]},{"property":"Melt mass-flow rate","domain":"physical","unit":"g/10 min","products":1,"lo":4,"hi":4,"median":4,"values":[4]},{"property":"Melt volume-flow rate","domain":"physical","unit":"cm³/10 min","products":1,"lo":20,"hi":20,"median":20,"values":[20]},{"property":"Mould shrinkage","domain":"physical","unit":"%","products":1,"lo":0.2,"hi":0.2,"median":0.2,"values":[0.2]},{"property":"Tensile strain at strength","domain":"mechanical","unit":"%","products":1,"lo":3,"hi":3,"median":3,"values":[3]},{"property":"Water absorption","domain":"physical","unit":"%","products":1,"lo":0.6,"hi":0.6,"median":0.6,"values":[0.6]}],"environment":[],"guide":null,"resin":null,"sources":[{"id":"D-BIGREP-HI-TEMP-CF-PAGE","publisher":"BigRep","title":"HI-TEMP CF - High Temperature Carbon Fiber 3D Printing","date":null,"read":"2026-09-21","kind":"Manufacturer product page or guide","url":"https://bigrep.com/filaments/hi-temp-cf/","note":"BigRep's product page for HI-TEMP CF, which calls it a PLA blend with 10 % chopped carbon fibre. Kept for the identity, never for properties."},{"id":"R-BIGREP-EZBYxVrNV7NGt4xXE3UWWuwBPYBbMpjmGobs-fcxZTeadg","publisher":"BigRep","title":"FILAMENT HI-TEMP CF","date":null,"read":"2026-09-26","kind":"Manufacturer TDS","url":"https://bigrepgmbh.sharepoint.com/:b:/g/EZBYxVrNV7NGt4xXE3UWWuwBPYBbMpjmGobs_fcxZTeadg?e=RWYSZA"},{"id":"R-EXTRUDR-PRINT-20260929-463457967aab","publisher":"Extrudr","title":"GreenTEC Pro CF – Carbon Composite Material for Performance | Extrudr","date":null,"read":"2026-09-29","kind":"Manufacturer product page or guide","url":"https://extrudr.com/en/at/products/greentec-pro-cf/","note":"The exact product's page, saved by the gap-fill research of and staged from that copy by digest (b40). Only the print setting its profile names was taken; the page's other statements are unread here."},{"id":"R-EXTRUDR-greentec-pro-cf-TDS-en","publisher":"Extrudr","title":"TECHNICAL DATA SHEET GREENTEC PRO CF","date":null,"read":"2026-09-26","kind":"Manufacturer TDS","url":"https://s3.extrudr.com/extrudr-media/datasheets/tds/tds-en/greentec-pro-cf-TDS-en.pdf"}]}